th another method. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 97 by 49:\n\nFirst, write 97 \u00d749.\n\nMultiply 97 by 9 (the ones digit): 9\u00d77=63, write down 3, carryover 6. 9\u00d79=81 +6=87. So first partial product is 873.\n\nThen multiply 97 by 40 (the tens digit is 4, so 4\u00d797 shifted one position to the left):\n\n4\u00d77=28, write 8, carryover 2. 4\u00d79=36 +2=38. So that gives 388, but shifted left once, so 3880.\n\nAdding 873 + 3880: 873 + 3880. Let me add 873 + 3000 = 3873, then +880 = 4753. So yes, that's correct. Therefore the product should be 4753. But wait, let me confirm with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, 97 \u00d749 can be calculated as (100 -3)(50 -1) = 100\u00d750 -100\u00d71 -3\u00d750 +3\u00d71 = 5000 -100 -150 +3= 5000-250+3=4753. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer is 4753. \n\nBut in my initial reasoning, I had some confusion with different numbers. I need to make sure I follow the correct numbers. The user's question is 97 and 49, so the answer is 4753. The steps should be as follows:\n\nMultiply 97 by 9 (ones place) to get 873. Multiply 97 by 40 (tens place) to get 3880. Sum them: 873 + 3880 = 4753.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning steps are correct once I applied the right numbers. I must have made a mistake in my initial thinking when I started with different numbers, but upon correcting, the process works out.\n</think>\n\n",
