n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 43 and 88?\n# Reasoning:\nLet\'s think step by step. 88 has two digits, so that we can reason in two steps.\n1. Multiply 43 by the ones place digit 8 of 88: 43 × 8 = 344.\n2. Multiply 43 by the tens place digit 80 of 88: 43 × 80 = 3440.\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 344 + 3440 = 3784.\nSo, the final computed product is 3784.\n\nYes, that looks correct. I think that\'s the way to go.\n'] 19%|#9        | 96/500 [1:10:31<8:54:26, 79.37s/it] 
