nce more. Let me compute 43\u00d788 step by step again:\n\n43 \u00d7 88:\n\nBreaking down 88 into 80 + 8:\n\nFirst part: 43 \u00d78 = (40\u00d78) + (3\u00d78) = 320 +24 = 344\n\nSecond part: 43 \u00d780 = (43\u00d78) \u00d710 = 344 \u00d710 = 3440\n\nAdding them: 344 + 3440. Let's add 344 + 3440:\n\n3440 + 300 = 3740\n\n3740 + 44 = 3784. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, if I use the vertical method:\n\n\u2003\u200343\n\u00d7\u00a088\n-------\n\u2003344\u2003 (43 \u00d7 8)\n+3440\u2003 (43 \u00d780 shifted left by one)\n-------\n\u20033784\n\nYes, so the final product is 3784. I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in the calculations now. The confusion earlier was because I was mixing up different numbers from previous examples, but now focusing on the given problem, it's straightforward. So the answer should be 3784.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 43 and 88 is \\boxed{3784}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 43 and 88, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps using the distributive property.\n\n1. Multiply 43 by the ones place digit of 88 (which is 8):\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 8 = (40 \\times 8) + (3 \\times 8) = 320 + 24 = 344\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 43 by the tens place digit of 88 (which is 80):\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 80 = (43 \\times 8) \\times 10 = 344 \\times 10 = 3440\n   \\]\n\n3. Sum the results of the two steps:\n   \\[\n   344 + 3440 = 3784\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{3784}\\).",
