ly, maybe using another method like standard multiplication:\n\n   92\n\nx29\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 92 by 9: 828\n\nThen multiply 92 by 20 (since the 2 is in the tens place, so 2*10=20), so 92*20=1840\n\nAdding them together gives 828+1840=2668. Yep, same result.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me confirm with another approach. 29 is 30-1, so 92*(30-1)=92*30 -92. 92*30 is 2760, minus 92 is 2760-92=2668. Yep, same answer. So that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
