e standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   42  \n× 71  \n------  \n   42 × 1 = 42  \n 42 × 70 = 2940 (shifted one position to the left)  \nAdding them: 42 + 2940 = 2982. That checks out.\n\nHmm, so the correct answer should be 2982. Let me make sure I didn't mix up any digits. The problem says 42 and 71, so yes. The initial thought process had some confusion with different numbers, but now it's corrected. Alright, I think that's solid.\n"]
