e.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 38 and 61?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 61 has two digits, so that we can reason in two steps.  \n1. Multiply 38 by the ones place digit 1 of 61:  \n   \\( 38 \\times 1 = 38 \\).  \n2. Multiply 38 by the tens place digit 60 of 61:  \n   \\( 38 \\times 60 = 2,\\!280 \\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 38 + 2,\\!280 = 2,\\!318 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{2318}\\).",
