uestion is:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 39 and 60?\n\nSo I need to solve 39×60.\n\nFollowing the same method.\n\nFirst, note that 60 has two digits: 6 and 0 (but in the tens place). So the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 39 by the ones place digit (0): 39×0=0.\n\n2. Multiply 39 by the tens place digit (6) but since it's in the tens place, it's 39×60=2340.\n\nSum the results: 0 + 2340 =2340.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning would be:\n\nLet's think step by step. 60 has two digits, so two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 39 by the ones place digit 0 of 60: 39×0=0.\n\n2. Multiply 39 by the tens place digit 60 of 60: 39×60=2340.\n\nSum all the step results: 0 + 2340 =2340.\n\nSo the final computed product is 2340.\n\nWait, but maybe the user wants the tens place digit to be considered as 6 (the digit), so the step would be 39×6 (the digit) multiplied by 10. So 39×6×10 =2340.\n\nAlternatively, the step would be written as 39×60.\n\nEither way, the steps are correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 2340.\n\nBut let me confirm by direct multiplication:\n\n39 × 60. Since 60 is 6×10, so 39×6=234, then ×10 is 2340. Correct.\n\nSo the steps are accurate.\n\nTherefore, the filled template should be as above.\n"]
