s per the template would be three steps? Wait, 22 is two digits, so maybe two steps? Let me check the original example they provided. \n\nIn the example with 27\u00d7153 (three digits), they had three steps. So for 22, which is two digits, the reasoning should have two steps. \n\nSo in the reasoning section, the user's template had for 153 (three digits):\n\n1. Multiply by ones place (3)\n\n2. Multiply by tens place (50)\n\n3. Multiply by hundreds place (100)\n\nHence, for 22 (two digits), the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply by the ones digit (2)\n\n2. Multiply by the tens digit (20)\n\nThen sum them. So the answer is 638. Alright, that's consistent. \n\nTherefore, the answer is 638. I think that's correct. Let me just verify with a calculator in my mind. 29\u00d720 is 580, plus 29\u00d72=58, so 580+58 is 638. Yes, that's right.\n</think>\n\n",
