. Wait, no. 2460 +41 is 2501?\n\nWait, 2460 plus 40 is 2500, plus 1 more is 2501. That seems right. \n\nBut let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n\u200341  \n×61  \n------  \n\u200341  (41 × 1)  \n2460  (41 × 60, shifted one position to the left)  \n------  \n2501  \n\nYes, that adds up to 2501. \n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property: (40 +1)(60 +1) = 40*60 + 40*1 +1*60 +1*1 = 2400 +40 +60 +1 = 2400+100+1=2501. \n\nYes, same result. So the correct answer is 2501. \n\nWait, but let me check once more with direct multiplication. 41 times 61. \n\nAlternatively, since 61 is close to 60, maybe 41*(60+1) = 41*60 +41 = 2460 +41=2501. Yep. \n\nOkay, so I think that's correct. The earlier confusion was because I was thinking of another problem, but now I'm focused. So the answer should be 2501.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 41 and 61 is \\boxed{2501}.\n"]
