ns places.\n1. Multiply 36 by the ones place digit (9):  \n   \\(36 \\times 9 = 324\\).  \n2. Multiply 36 by the tens place digit (40):  \n   \\(36 \\times 40 = 1,440\\).  \nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(324 + 1,440 = 1,764\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **1,764**.",
