3\u00d72=86.\n\n2. Multiply 43 by the tens place digit 70 of 72 (since the 7 is in the tens place, it's 7\u00d710). So 43\u00d770=3010.\n\nThen sum those two results: 86 + 3010 = 3096.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 3096. I think that's correct. Let me confirm with another approach, like the lattice method or another multiplication check.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard algorithm again:\n\n\u2003\u00a043\n\u00d7\u00a072\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2003\u00a086  (43\u00d72)\n+3010 (43\u00d770, shifted one position to the left)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u20033096\n\nYes, that's correct. So the answer is 3096.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 43 and 72 is \\boxed{3096}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 43 and 72, we can break down the multiplication using the place values of the digits in 72. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 43 by the ones place digit (2) of 72:**\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 2 = 86\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 43 by the tens place digit (70) of 72:**\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 70 = 43 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 301 \\times 10 = 3010\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two steps:**\n   \\[\n   86 + 3010 = 3096\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 43 and 72 is \\(\\boxed{3096}\\).",
