 digit as 71 (since 629 had a 3 in the tens place, so 31). So here, for the tens place digit of 2 in 63, it's 65. So that part is correct.\n\nThen, after getting both products, I need to add them together. So 189 (from the ones place) plus 5502 (from the tens place) equals.. Let me add those. 549 + 3856. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
