stributive property: 61 × (50 + 3) = (61 × 50) + (61 × 3).\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n61 × 50: 61 times 5 is 305, so times 10 is 3050.\n\n61 × 3: 60×3=180 and 1×3=3, so total 183.\n\nAdding them together: 3050 + 183 = 3233.\n\nWait, that seems right. Let me verify with another method. Using standard multiplication:\n\n\u2003\xa061  \n×\xa053  \n──────  \nMultiply 61 by 3: 183  \nMultiply 61 by 50: 3050  \nAdd them: 183 + 3050 = 3233. Yes, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, using the box method: (60 +1)(50 +3) = 60×50 + 60×3 +1×50 +1×3 = 3000 + 180 +50 +3 = 3000+233=3233. Correct.\n\nSo the final answer should be 3233. I need to present this following the template\'s structure, showing each step as in the example.\n\nThe example had three steps because the second number was three digits, but since 53 is two digits, there are two steps: multiplying by the ones (3) and the tens (50). So the reasoning steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 61 by 3 (the ones place).\n2. Multiply 61 by 50 (the tens place).\nThen sum the results.\n']
