80.\n\nNow, add the two results together: 288 + 7,680.\n\nAdding those: 7,680 + 200 = 7,880; then +88 = 7,968. \n\nWait, let me confirm:\n\n288 +7,680: \n\n7,680 + 200 = 7,880\n\n7,880 + 88 = 7,968. Yes.\n\nAlternatively, 7,680 + 288:\n\n7,680 + 200 = 7,880\n\n7,880 + 88 = 7,968. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 96 and 83 is 7,968.\n\nWait, let me check with another method to be sure. Using the standard algorithm:\n\nMultiply 96 by 83.\n\nFirst, write:\n\n\u2003\u200396  \n× 83  \n—————  \nMultiply 96 by 3: 288  \n\nMultiply 96 by 80: 7,680 (since 96×8=768, then ×10)\n\nAdd them: 288 +7,680 = 7,968. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:\n\n(90 +6)(80 +3) = 90×80 +90×3 +6×80 +6×3\n\n90×80=7,200\n\n90×3=270\n\n6×80=480\n\n6×3=18\n\nAdding all together: 7,200 +270 = 7,470; 7,470 +480 =7,950; 7,950 +18=7,968. Same result. \n\nSo the final answer is 7,968. \n\nI think that's solid. Now, I need to present this in the template provided. The user's example had three steps because the second number had three digits, but since 83 is two digits, there will be two steps. Let me structure the reasoning accordingly.\n"]
